0/hvVtcMr1LY03tOFuUG63heR3KNd.jpg\",\"rating\":5,\"year\":2025,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.2077922077922078,\"_genreOverlap\":1},{\"id\":214477,\"title\":\"The Illegal Trip\",\"poster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/7n4DFKOrtK3du9JbvXNwiU2GTVD.jpg\",\"rating\":0,\"year\":2021,\"type\":\"tv\",\"_score\":0.20674157303370788,\"_genreOverlap\":1}],\"seasonNumber\":13,\"seasonName\":\"Season 13\",\"seasonOverview\":\"\",\"seasonPoster\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/l01tfkunPY0LEVZiENIvVF9XOyr.jpg\",\"seasonAirDate\":\"2018-10-17\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"Episode 1\",\"overview\":\"Drew decides that he needs something different to stand out from the competition. He and Tee head to Italy hoping to find some antiques that his rivals won't be able to match.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-10-17\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Episode 2\",\"overview\":\"At a giant mid-Wales market, Drew has the pick of over 1000 stalls showcasing world-class pieces. He spies a 200-year-old Windsor chair in the best condition he’s ever seen.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-10-24\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Episode 3\",\"overview\":\"Drew is on a road trip, travelling to Norfolk, Pembroke and Essex. In Pembroke, he finds an old church that has been converted into an antiques store with a varied selection.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-10-31\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"Episode 4\",\"overview\":\"In a quiet South London suburb, Drew comes face to face with the most extraordinary collection of American automobilia he’s ever seen, including Evel Knievel’s Messerschmitt.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-11-07\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Episode 5\",\"overview\":\"His hunt for fresh stock takes Drew to the Cotswolds, where he finds a giant stash of Indian and Afghan treasures which have come directly from the subcontinent.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-11-14\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Episode 6\",\"overview\":\"Drew heads to a huge antiques wholesaler in Exeter, where he finds pile upon pile of affordable gems. Next, it’s on to north London, to visit an emporium of curiosities.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-11-21\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"Episode 7\",\"overview\":\"Drew heads to Devon, where he finds a wealth of unusual oddities housed in a country pub. Next, it’s on to Hastings, which has enjoyed a recent resurgence in the antiques trade.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2018-11-28\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"Episode 8\",\"overview\":\"Modern day treasure hunter Drew Pritchard travels the length and breadth of the UK in search of weird and wonderful objects. The bigger the hoard, the happier he is.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-02-20\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Episode 9\",\"overview\":\"Modern day treasure hunter Drew Pritchard travels the length and breadth of the UK in search of weird and wonderful objects. The bigger the hoard, the happier he is.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-02-27\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"Episode 10\",\"overview\":\"In Sussex, Drew has some incredible luck when he is offered first pick of a shop packed full of French items. Then in Kent, he's invited behind the scenes of a historic railway.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-06\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"Episode 11\",\"overview\":\"Modern day treasure hunter Drew Pritchard travels the length and breadth of the UK in search of weird and wonderful objects. The bigger the hoard, the happier he is.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-13\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"Episode 12\",\"overview\":\"Sensing the chance to get some bargains, Drew Pritchard checks in on some contacts who are downsizing and selling off collections. In Norwich, he finds a beautiful Victorian umbrella stand.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-20\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"Episode 13\",\"overview\":\"Drew Pritchard examines furniture in a Black Country factory. Next, in Derby, a new contact pays off when he finds the crankshaft from a Battle of Britain fighter plane.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-03-27\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":14,\"name\":\"Episode 14\",\"overview\":\"In Lancashire, Drew Pritchard visits a sprawling salvage yard that yields many unique items. Next, at an auction house, he faces off against other dealers in a bidding war.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-04-03\",\"runtime\":45},{\"number\":15,\"name\":\"Episode 15\",\"overview\":\"Drew Pritchard visits some family-run businesses in Lincolnshire and Norfolk in the hope of finding rare and unusual antiques that have never been put on sale before.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2019-04-10\",\"runtime\":45}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2011-11-14\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}